       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, about 214 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is in the range where acetaminophen causes acute liver injury and failure, and I can't think of a therapeutic use for it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO four times daily (2.6 g/day). Give me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Route this to pharmacy.** If something unusual is going on, a pharmacist or toxicology can review it. Examples are a different intended drug or unit, or a patient who needs a nonstandard regimen.\n- **Treat a possible ingestion.** If you're concerned about an acetaminophen overdose, that needs a level and NAC protocol rather than a scheduled order. Poison Control is 1-800-222-1222 in the US.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
     ],
